WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.524
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Thirty-One.

2
00:00:03.524 --> 00:00:07.345
Construct through a given point a line parallel to a given line.

3
00:00:07.345 --> 00:00:10.748
Let A be the given point, and segment B C the given line.

4
00:00:10.748 --> 00:00:14.330
We construct through point A a line parallel to segment B C.

5
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:19.852
Take a point D at random on segment B C, and construct segment A D.

6
00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:28.152
By Proposition Twenty-Three, on segment D A and at point A on it, construct angle D A E equal to angle A D C.

7
00:00:28.152 --> 00:00:31.960
Then extend segment E A in a straight line to A F.

8
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:44.383
Since transversal A D falling on segments B C and E F makes the alternate interior angles D A E and A D C equal, by Proposition Twenty-Seven, segment E F is parallel to segment B C.

9
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:52.540
Therefore through the given point A, line E A F has been constructed parallel to the given line B C, as was required to do.
